# Commit message format

All commits must follow this pattern (enforced by Husky `commit-msg` hook):

```
[type] PW-123 description
```

## Pre-commit checks (Husky `pre-commit`)

Every commit runs these in order — all must pass:

1. **lint-staged** — ESLint + Prettier on staged files
2. **type-check** — `tsc --noEmit`
3. **build** — `next build`

Run manually: `pnpm precommit`

## Allowed types

| Type | When to use |
|---|---|
| `feat` | New feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `hotfix` | Urgent production fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Formatting, no logic change |
| `refactor` | Code change, no feature/fix |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `chore` | Tooling, deps, config |
| `ci` | CI/CD changes |
| `revert` | Revert a prior commit |

## Ticket (required)

- Must be `PW-{number}` immediately after the type tag
- Examples: `PW-11`, `PW-142`

## Examples

```
[feat] PW-11 add product detail gallery
[fix] PW-42 correct cart quantity on reload
[hotfix] PW-99 patch checkout redirect loop
[chore] PW-7 update commitlint rules
```

## Rules

- Square brackets around type: `[feat]` not `feat`
- Single space between `[type]`, ticket, and description
- No period at the end of the subject
- Use imperative mood: "add" not "added"
